{{Quote|Every Geonosian building has a series of catacombs beneath it that run deep underground.|[[Jedi General]] [[Luminara Unduli]]|audio=BlowTheFactory-WF.flac|<ref name="WF">{{TCW|Weapons Factory}}</ref>}}
[[File:GeonosianUndead-LoT.jpg|right|thumb|220x220px|Undead Geonosians in the catacombs]]
The '''Geonosian catacombs''',<ref name="A Jedi's Duty">{{StoryCite|story=A Jedi's Duty|book=Stories of Jedi and Sith}}</ref> also known as the '''Geonosis catacombs''',<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis episode guide">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/ghosts-of-geonosis-episode-guide|text="Ghosts of Geonosis" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Rebels}}</ref> the '''Catacombs of Geonosis''',<ref name="Scene to Stats">{{AtomicMassGames|url=transmission/scene-to-stats-geonosian-warriors|text=Scene to Stats: Geonosian Warriors}}</ref> or the '''Geonosis caves''',<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|klik-klak|Klik-Klak}}</ref> were a massive tunnel networks located beneath the surface of [[Geonosis]]. Every [[Geonosian]] building had a series of catacombs beneath it.<ref name="WF" />

During the [[Second Battle of Geonosis]], [[Padawan]]s [[Barriss Offee]] and [[Ahsoka Tano]] of the [[Jedi Order]] went through the catacombs to reach the [[reactor]] of the [[Geonosis primary droid foundry]].<ref name="WF" /> [[Galactic Republic]] [[Republic Military|forces]] would later traverse through the catacombs under the [[Progate Temple]], and the [[Jedi]] and [[clone trooper]]s would come face to face with [[Karina the Great]], [[queen]] of the [[Geonosian]]s.<ref name="LOT">{{TCW|Legacy of Terror}}</ref>

